  "raw": {
    "pillar": "Interesting Facts",
    "headline": "WTF? Did we just discover a new million-person civilization in the Amazon?",
    "challenge": "The Amazon rainforest has long been shrouded in mystery, with its dense canopy and unnavigable floor making research difficult. One of the victims of this was the Aquiry civilization, an ancient Amazonian civilization whose history researchers were mostly blind to. Until now.",
    "solution": "Nature reports that researchers use advanced LiDAR technology to discover hundreds of geoglyphs previously lost to time. These monumental, geometric earthworks span an area of about 183,000 km2. This suggests the Aquiry civilization was much more than a primitive tribe as previously hypothesized.",
    "resultHeading": "The Aquiry may have numbered as many as 3 million at their zenith!",
    "resultLine": "The findings suggest a complex societal structure and a population of 1.5 to 3 million. Read more at the link in my bio!",
    "whyMatters": "This discovery challenges our understanding of precolonial Amazonian societies, revealing a sophisticated civilization that thrived for over 1,500 years. It also highlights the importance of advanced technology in uncovering the mysteries of our past.",
    "engagementQuestion": "What secrets of the ancient world can new technologies discover next?",
    "captionLead": "Scientists just uncovered a massive ancient civilization hidden beneath the Amazon’s thick canopy. Using LiDAR technology, they found hundreds of monumental earthworks—geoglyphs—built by the Aquiry, revealing a million-person society much more complex than we ever imagined.",
    "storyHashtag": "Archaeology",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10835-7",
