  "reel": {
    "script": "The Amazon’s hiding something big. Literally. Scientists just found hundreds of ancient earthworks under the trees. They used LiDAR tech to spot these huge, geometric shapes. Turns out, the Aquiry civilization was way bigger than we thought. Thousands of these geoglyphs were discovered. At its peak, up to 3 million people lived there. This changes what we know about precolonial Amazonian societies. It also shows how cool tech can help us uncover history. What do you think these geoglyphs were used for?",
    "hook": "WTF?! Did Scientists Just Discover a Million-Person Society?",
    "mood": "curious",
    "wordCount": 82,
    "lines": [
      {
        "text": "So yeah. The Amazons thick canopy has been hiding something big!"
      },
      {
        "text": "Literally."
      },
      {
        "text": "Scientists knew about an ancient Amazonian society called the Aquiry, but considered them small and primitive."
      },
      {
        "text": "Turns out that was totally off base thanks to new surveys using LiDAR, who spotted  huge, geometric shapes indicating a much larger society in the jungle."
      },
      {
        "text": "So turns out, the Aquiry civilization was way bigger than we thought. Like up to 3 million, bigger."
      },
      {
        "text": "Thousands of these geoglyphs were discovered."
      },
      {
        "text": "Researchers are completely rethinking this society now."
      },
      {
        "text": "Further studies are needed, but looks like there could have been many complex Amazonian societies existing for centuries"
      },
      {
        "text": "It also shows how new tech can help us uncover history in ways we never thought possible."
      },
      {
        "text": "Where do you think we should use this tech next?"
      }
    ],
